					"name": "Protection from Evil/Good",
					"tags": [
						"Regular"
					],
					"vtt_notes": "It provides Protection as Armor (p. B253) and Magic Resistance (Magic, p. 123), but only against direct attacks and spells originating from genuinely Evil or Good beings (as determined by the GM). Indirect effects—such as traps or mindless golems—never count, even if they are ultimately the Devil’s work. Each energy point invested (up to 5) grants +1 DR and +2 Magic Resistance. The subject of the spell must be willing, or the spell automatically fails.",
